TEXT 200 96 Left 1 ;+5 V DRIVE RAIL
TEXT 200 640 Left 1 ;GATE NODE  -  this is what the driver charges
TEXT 200 1288 Left 1 ;OFF RAIL  -  0 V or -2 V
TEXT 200 40 Left 3 ;INSIDE THE SEGMENTED GATE DRIVER  -  contents of models/segdrv.lib
TEXT 224 560 Left 2 ;EIGHT PULL-UP SLICES  -  each 8 ohm, slice i on when npu >= i.  How hard the device is switched ON.
TEXT 224 1120 Left 2 ;EIGHT PULL-DOWN SLICES  -  each 8 ohm, slice i on when npd >= i.  How hard it is switched OFF.
TEXT 1544 1168 Left 2 ;MILLER CLAMP  -  0.5 ohm
TEXT 1814 904 Left 1 ;the GaN gate
TEXT 200 1400 Left 2 !.model SWP SW(Ron=0.01 Roff=1e9 Vt=0.5 Vh=0.05)
TEXT 200 1426 Left 2 !.param npu=8 npd=8 runit=8 rclamp=0.5
TEXT 200 1452 Left 2 !.param VDRV=5 VNEG=0
TEXT 200 1478 Left 2 !Vvp vp 0 DC {VDRV}
TEXT 200 1504 Left 2 !Vvn vn 0 DC {VNEG}
TEXT 200 1530 Left 2 !Vpu pu 0 PULSE(0 1 0 1n 1n 200n 500n)
TEXT 200 1556 Left 2 !Vpd pd 0 PULSE(1 0 0 1n 1n 200n 500n)
TEXT 200 1582 Left 2 !Vclk clk 0 DC 0
TEXT 200 1608 Left 2 !.tran 0.1n 1u
TEXT 200 1634 Left 2 !.meas TRAN vgate_high MAX V(out)
TEXT 200 1680 Left 2 ;npu and npd are the slice counts the FPGA sets. Press Run to see the gate charge.
